  with an open-ended, neo-Kantian evolutionary framework. Bernstein is shown
  to have rejected the Zusammenbruchstheorie not primarily on empirical grounds
  but on philosophical ones: the idea of historical necessity was incompatible
  with the normative, voluntarist dimension of socialist politics. Steger
  traces the influence of British Fabianism, neo-Kantian ethics (Cohen,
